            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Customization works as expected here. You can verify it via `:=MiniIcons.get('filetype', 'htmldjango')`.\r\n\r\nThe problem is that detection of 'htmldjango' filetype [relies on the file content](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/65a703e06063c85c3dd5fdb3ad4e1207a622ef30/runtime/lua/vim/filetype/detect.lua#L732-L737), while 'file' and 'extension' categories in 'mini.icons' can use only supplied file name (or preferably full file path).\r\n\r\nAs both 'neo-tree.nvim' and (what looks like) 'lualine.nvim' compute icon data based on the file name or path, they display the icon for 'html' filetype. If 'lualine.nvim' used the filetype (as does 'mini.statusline', for example), it would have shown the '==' as icon. ",
